  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "spotlight",
      "item": "tribalpower:willow_sapling",
      "title": "The Weeping Colossus",
      "text": [
        "The greatest thing that grows in the March. Weeping Colossi stand in **groves of two to eight** across the Reed Fen, the Highlands and the Steppe. Each is **over a hundred blocks tall**, its hollow trunk as wide as a hall at the root, its arching limbs letting fall curtains of **Willow Strands** that reach toward the ground.",
        "Plant **four Willow Saplings in a square** to raise a colossus of your own. A single sapling grows a young willow."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "spotlight",
      "item": "tribalpower:willow_strand",
      "title": "Willow Strands",
      "text": [
        "Strands hang from leaves and from each other. **You can climb them**, so a colossus is a ladder to its own crown. Cut the leaves above and the whole curtain falls. Shears keep a strand; a few tips carry a **glowing seed**."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "The other trees",
      "text": [
        "- **Hearthoak**: a squat, broad giant of the Steppe. Warm honey wood with knots.",
        "- **Bellcap**: a thin trunk under a violet bell of blossom, in the Crystal Fields. Pale lilac wood.",
        "- **Frostpine**: tall and straight, with flat tiers of needles; the Snow Fields and Highlands. Rosy wood.",
        "- **Cinderwood**: the scorched, leaning snag of the Ember Wastes. Its dark wood **does not burn**.",
        "- **Strider**: stands above the fen water on arching stilt roots. Silvery sea-green wood."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Wood of your own",
      "text": [
        "Every one of these trees has its own wood and its own sapling, which drops from its leaves. Each wood makes planks, stairs, slabs, a fence and gate, a door, a trapdoor, a pressure plate and a button, and an axe strips its logs like any other. They work in every recipe that takes planks or logs."
      ]
    }
  ]
